{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-346462",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let $A$ denote the area under the curve $y=r(t)$ over $[0,18].$ In this case, we have $n=5$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the area is computed as \n\n$$\nA≈r(4)Δ{t}_{1}+r(7)Δ{t}_{2}+r(10)Δ{t}_{3}+r(13)Δ{t}_{4}+r(18)Δ{t}_{5},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{t}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $t$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{t}_{i}={t}_{i}-{t}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δt$'s.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $4$ | $7$ | $10$ | $13$ | $18$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δt$ | $-$ | $4$ | $3$ | $3$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| $r(t)$ | $-$ | $5$ | $3$ | $4$ | $2$ | $1$ |\n\nWe plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈5\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =20+9+12+6+5 \\\\  & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total accumulation of medication. So, the total medication delivered is $52$ milligrams.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
